---
description: Build a purpose-limited disclosure from reviewed source spans, verified sanitization receipts, and a rendered output bound to the approved recipient.
args: { request: DisclosureReviewRequest, evidence: DisclosureEvidencePack }
returns: DisclosureReleaseProposal
uses: [disclosureDesk/resolveDisclosureScope, disclosureDesk/selectContestedSpans, disclosureDesk/mapCombinedInference, disclosureDesk/preserveQualifierContext, disclosureDesk/sanitizeTextAndMetadata, disclosureDesk/verifyRenderedArtifact, disclosureDesk/checkRecipientApproval, disclosureDesk/mapChallengeToSources]
---
1. Bind saved = evidence.checkpoint when present, otherwise null. Bind scope = resolveDisclosureScope(request, evidence.cases, evidence.policyCandidates). Unresolved authority, recipient, purpose or date window blocks affected documents before span selection.
2. Bind selections = selectContestedSpans(scope, evidence.documentInspections). Retain each source hash and locator. Bind plan = mapCombinedInference(selections, evidence.documentInspections) across the assembled fragments, then qualifiedPlan = preserveQualifierContext(selections, plan, evidence.documentInspections). If a truthful qualifier is itself restricted, withhold the statement and explain the limitation.
3. Bind sanitizedReceipts = sanitizeTextAndMetadata(qualifiedPlan, evidence.redactionReceipts, evidence.documentInspections). These are verified receipts, not a redaction plan. Each must bind the selected source hash and exact redaction map to sanitized output with both text layers and metadata covered. No receipt means no artifact.
4. Bind verifiedArtifacts = verifyRenderedArtifact(request, sanitizedReceipts, evidence.renderReceipts). Retain only artifacts with exact document/output identity, visual review and no residual findings. Rendering alone grants no recipient authority.
5. Bind approvals = checkRecipientApproval(request, verifiedArtifacts, evidence.recipientApprovals). A changed recipient, purpose or rendered artifact hash requires approval for that exact new binding. A prior approval on different bytes cannot authorize these artifacts.
6. Bind challengeMap = mapChallengeToSources(verifiedArtifacts, selections, qualifiedPlan, approvals, evidence.challengeMappings). Preserve the immutable path from each candidate released span to source hash, redaction basis and exact approval. Keep unresolved challenges explicit instead of inventing source locators.
7. Bind withheldDocuments to requested document IDs lacking a verified artifact or exact approval, plus documents affected by scope.blockers, unresolved inference mitigation, qualifier loss or challengeMap.withheldDocumentIds. An unresolved document-level risk with no defensible narrower scope withholds that document; an unresolved release-wide scope withholds the whole requested set. Bind artifacts to the verifiedArtifacts whose document is not withheld and whose renderedHash occurs in approvals.authorizedArtifactHashes. Bind readyForAuthorizedRelease to true only when artifacts is nonempty, scope has no blockers, every returned artifact is authorized for this recipient/purpose/hash, and none belongs to withheldDocuments. Partial disclosure may be ready only for that explicit authorized subset; missing documents remain listed.
8. Bind checkpoint = reconcileDisclosureCheckpoint(saved, request, evidence, scope, selections, qualifiedPlan, artifacts, approvals, challengeMap). Preserve prior authorized release bindings and actual dispatch receipts without asserting a new dispatch. Return { caseId: request.caseId, recipientId: request.recipientId, purpose: request.purpose, scope, plan: qualifiedPlan, artifacts, withheldDocuments, unresolvedChallenges: challengeMap.unresolvedChallenges, readyForAuthorizedRelease, checkpoint } as DisclosureReleaseProposal. The caller can review exact withheld reasons and supply a new source, render or approval in the next invocation.
